\title{RcppOptimLib: An Interface to the C++ Numerical Optimization Library
'OptimLib'}
\description{
Ships the header-only version of Keith O'Hara's 'OptimLib'
(\url{https://optimlib.readthedocs.io/}) so that R users and other R
packages can use its optimization algorithms (BFGS, L-BFGS, conjugate
gradient, gradient descent, Nelder-Mead, differential evolution,
particle swarm, and root finding) from C++ code via 'Rcpp' and
'RcppArmadillo'.
}
\details{
There are two ways to use the package:
\enumerate{
\item \strong{From C++ (recommended):} add \verb{LinkingTo: RcppOptimLib, Rcpp, RcppArmadillo} to your package's DESCRIPTION and
\verb{PKG_LIBS = $(LAPACK_LIBS) $(BLAS_LIBS) $(FLIBS)} to its
\code{src/Makevars} (or use
\verb{// [[Rcpp::depends(RcppOptimLib, RcppArmadillo)]]} in a
\code{sourceCpp()} file), then \verb{#include <RcppOptimLib.h>} and call the
\verb{optim::} routines directly on Armadillo vectors.
\item \strong{From R:} call the demonstration wrappers such as
\code{\link[=optim_sphere_bfgs]{optim_sphere_bfgs()}}, \code{\link[=optim_ackley_de]{optim_ackley_de()}}, \code{\link[=optimlib_bfgs]{optimlib_bfgs()}} and
\code{\link[=optimlib_nm]{optimlib_nm()}}. The latter two accept plain R functions as
objectives via callbacks.
}
